}# Godwyn move-set physics audit

Each section is appended only after its move has been rendered, visually reviewed and encoded. Source: a read-only copy of `models/astra_character_v2_prechar2.blend` retained as `models/astra_move_character_base.blend` so concurrent character-track edits cannot change the base between moves. No source character/X-slash/cinematography files are modified.

## Method and limitations

Same kinematic method as `renders/astra/naturalness_audit.md`: 121 bones sampled at quarter-frame intervals, shortest quaternion-log angular velocity (antipodal signs are equivalent), integer-frame angular acceleration and reversal/spike candidates. Candidate thresholds: reversal dot < −0.5 with both steps > 0.5°; speed > max(4°/frame, 2.8× local seven-sample median); acceleration > 12°/frame². These are screening thresholds, not torque limits.

Anatomy uses actual joint heads rather than the imported display tails. Elbow/knee flexion is zero at straight; wrist screening compares forearm and hand longitudinal axes. Broad screening thresholds are 150° elbow flexion and 80° wrist bend. Shoulder elevation, segment-length errors, asymmetric left/right speed correlations, blade tip speed and floor clearance are retained in per-move metrics. This is not a calibrated anatomical or muscle/torque simulation. Sword-mass sensitivity additionally tests 2%, 4% and 6% of body mass, with sword COM 45% from hilt to tip; results are in `<move>_sword_mass_sensitivity.json`.

COM uses torso 49.7%, head 8.1%, and each thigh 10%, shank 4.65%, foot 1.45%, upper arm 2.8%, forearm 1.6%, hand 0.6%. Segment centers and support hull match the prior audit (20 cm boot width, 12 cm heel extension, 9 cm toe extension, 2 cm inset). Grounded support requires an intended planted foot and measured sole clearance below 15 mm. Static COM outside that hull is disclosed; a caught step or flight is identified explicitly, not labelled statically stable.

Sole and hem clearance is measured on the evaluated skinned body mesh at every integer frame against Z = −0.015 m. Foot targets are corrected from measured sole height; distal cloth locations gather cloth upward while waist and upper chain roots remain attached. Corrections, before/after values and all angular flags remain in `<move>_contacts.json` and `<move>_metrics.json`. No hidden cloth/body triangle collision certification is claimed. Cloth is a deterministic delayed/damped kinematic response, not a fabric simulation.

Loop clips bake the duplicate endpoint in the blend but omit it from the MP4 to avoid a held seam frame. World pose equality is checked modulo any documented root displacement; quarter-frame finite-difference seam velocities are reported. Render: Blender 5.2.1, Metal, BLENDER_EEVEE, 768×768, 30 fps. The stable pre-char2 character is used without the later face/hair track or its material workarounds. Contact sheets contain labelled frames, with every second active frame for attacks. MP4s are libx264/yuv420p and fully decoded for validation.

## idle_guard — completed

96 rendered frames / 3.2 seconds, plus duplicate F97 in the blend. The stable prechar2 binding preserves all 326,095 authored bone keys (action SHA-256 `fbf0c7108313fbe1e5476a2944d962c9db558f8ca47e68ff0e7a1f53a2e6613b`). The stable source/snapshot SHA-256 is `de09639b845c1cfe6c167737de8a53010980c8c9126748f7520b22f0fa2a608e`.

- **Continuity/anatomy:** 385 quarter-frame samples, 121 bones, zero angular candidate flags. Peak local angular step 0.367°/frame; peak acceleration 0.0302°/frame². Right elbow 35.01–46.09°, wrist 26.34–29.18°; left elbow 67.89–74.49°, wrist 18.83–19.13°. Knees remain bent approximately 25–32°. Maximum measured limb-length error is 0.0048 mm.
- **Loop and weight:** F1/F97 pose mismatch is zero. Opposite-sided quarter-frame finite-difference velocity mismatch is 1.93 mm/s and 0.088°/s (finite sampling of a continuous curved cycle). Support margin stays at least 15.36 cm inside the inset hull. Left/right arm speed correlation is 0.60, forearm 0.73 and hand 0.65; the off shoulder has a separate delay. The pelvis initiates weight transfer; chest, shoulders and wrist have successive phase offsets rather than a rigid shared sine. This is a restrained guard, not a torque-producing attack.
- **Contact fixes:** raw sole hover was 7.7–11.7 mm. Final stable-source soles: left 2.00–2.03 mm, right 1.54–1.70 mm. The initial hem sank up to about 7 cm; two measured distal gathering passes removed it. The final lowest sampled hem is 0.031 mm above the stage. No sampled foot/hem penetration remains.
- **Blade/cloth:** blade tip remains at least 9.50 cm above Z=0 and drifts 16.79 cm laterally through a curved, non-constant-speed loop; peak speed 0.179 m/s. All 97 secondary chains move. Central robe/cape yaw response best matches the hips at +6/+8 frames over the tested lag interval. The cloth drifts and settles continuously at the loop boundary.

### Sword grip coherence

The source binding was already rigid, but the close-up failed visually: blue material faces and an inner-cuff strip obscured an overly open imported grasp. The derived-only `astra_move_grip_fix.py` assigns 3,442 hand-region faces to the existing gauntlet gold, removes the 621-face inner-cuff strip located by camera-ray probes, and closes 2,553 existing finger/hand vertices around the measured hilt envelope. Maximum source-space adjustment is 10.57 cm on this 3.2 m character. Those vertices bind exclusively to RightHand. This is a static grasp repair; bone keys and the protected character input are unchanged. No replacement fingers, weapon mesh or independent sword animation are introduced.

At all 385 quarter frames the hilt-to-wrist distance is 165.3152–165.3156 mm: variation **0.00042 mm**. Hand-local hilt drift is at most **0.000475 mm**; evaluated sword-tip error is **0.000573 mm**. Every sword vertex remains RightHand=1 through one Armature modifier, with no sword action or constraints. Across all 97 integer frames, 2,256 evaluated closed-hand vertices drift at most **0.000905 mm** in hand space. The source's pre-armature surface polish changes nominal rest positions by up to 14.99 mm; that fixed shape offset is explicitly separated from temporal drift.

Close-ups F1/F49/F97 were inspected: the fingers close around the hilt, the cuff strip no longer crosses it, and no visible finger/hilt gap, detach or independent blade roll remains. One-handed throughout; the off hand stays at the waist. Cutting-edge alignment is not an active-cut condition in this low-hang loop. The source gauntlet has fused sculpted finger detail, so this does not assert separately articulated phalanx motion.

**Visual/video verification:** inspected the stable-source test still, all three grip close-ups, the final 13-frame contact sheet and frames decoded from the actual MP4. H.264/yuv420p, 768×768, 30 fps, exactly 96 frames; full decode passed. Native motion blur is disabled for this subtle loop. Remaining limits: kinematic cloth and COM proxies, no hidden full-body triangle-collision or torque certification. Evidence: `idle_guard_metrics.json`, `idle_guard_contacts.json`, `idle_guard_grip_metrics.json`, `idle_guard_rebind.json`, `idle_guard_video_verification.json`.

**Sword-mass sensitivity:** at 2%/4%/6%, idle support minima remain +161.20/+168.50/+175.53 mm inside the inset hull; no outside frames.

## walk_stalk — completed

72 rendered frames / 2.4 seconds, duplicate F73; 1.08 m forward root displacement per cycle. Camera and lights track that displacement. The same frozen prechar2 source and derived grasp repair are reused.

- **Continuity/anatomy:** 289 quarter-frame samples across 121 bones. Peak local step 7.065°/frame, acceleration 2.533°/frame². One small reversal candidate remains: RightUpLeg F59, 0.580°/frame and 0.995°/frame², at the normal swing flexion/extension transition. Initial reach-clamping defects produced eight candidates and 12.9°/frame; lowering the pelvis and narrowing the stance removed those defects. Knees L20.01–65.75°/R24.54–68.66°, elbows L76.89–80.91°/R43.94–56.79°, wrists L18.82–19.24°/R31.20–32.99°. Segment-length error below 0.006 mm.
- **Contact fixes:** replacing the constant swing offset with measured correction through the entire step removed approximately 20 mm of landing hover/penetration. Final planted soles L1.745–2.501 mm/R2.493–2.734 mm; minimum across swing and stance 1.672 mm. Planted ankle planar movement below 0.001 mm/frame. Lowest evaluated hem +0.946 mm.
- **Balance/weight:** the pelvis shifts over the supporting leg before each swing, with asymmetric upper-body phase offsets and an active low sword. COM lies outside the conservative inset support hull at F28–31 and F67 only. Worst margin −39.70 mm at F31, recovered by the next frame's left-foot landing; the other event reaches −10.35 mm at F67 and is caught at F68. The longest exception is four frames (0.133 s). These are explicitly caught-by-step intervals, not static equilibrium.
- **Loop:** root-relative endpoint error 0.000721 mm, orientation error zero. Analytically matched Bezier endpoint slopes differ by at most 0.0671 mm/s in location and 0.0000263 quaternion components/s. Opposite-sided quarter-frame velocity estimates differ by 53.37 mm/s and 8.34°/s because they sample opposite curvature; those are not the common endpoint derivatives. Both tangent gates pass.
- **Blade/cloth/asymmetry:** tip stays at least 54.17 mm above Z=0, with approximately 2.09 m/s peak world speed including travel/weight transfer. All 97 secondary bones move; central robe/cape best-fit yaw lag +5/+1 frames. The cape trails forward travel and settles between footfalls. Left/right arm, forearm and hand speed correlations are approximately −0.16/−0.03/+0.11, avoiding mirrored timing.

### Sword grip coherence

The rigid RightHand-only sword binding passes every quarter frame. Hilt/wrist distance 165.31510–165.31549 mm (variation **0.000389 mm**), hand-local hilt drift **0.000461 mm**, evaluated blade-tip error **0.000571 mm**. All 2,256 audited evaluated closed-hand vertices remain fixed in wrist space within **0.000848 mm** over all 73 integer frames. Same static derived hand correction as idle_guard; no two-handed moments.

Inspected close-ups at the two opposing step phases F19/F55: closed gold gauntlet around the grip, no visible gap, cuff intrusion, independent roll or detachment. Five close-ups F1/F19/F37/F55/F73 are retained. The low sword remains point-down with a relaxed, slightly changing wrist rather than a pendulum arm swing. No active cutting-edge test applies to locomotion.

**Visual/video verification:** inspected the revised preview, final evenly sampled contact sheet and actual decoded MP4 sheet. The weighted footfalls, low wrist and trailing cloth remain readable; the stable hair and materials remain clean. H.264/yuv420p, 768×768, 30 fps, 72 frames; full decode passed. Residuals are the disclosed small knee reversal and caught-by-step COM intervals, plus the shared kinematic-model limits. Evidence: `walk_stalk_metrics.json`, `walk_stalk_contacts.json`, `walk_stalk_grip_metrics.json`, `walk_stalk_video_verification.json`.

**Sword-mass sensitivity:** 2%/4%/6% minima are −44.78/−49.67/−54.37 mm, mainly at the late left-foot catch. The hypothetical 6% mass also moves COM at most 3.01 mm outside the actual, non-inset boot hull during F48–65 (23.01 mm outside the 20 mm inset). This small sustained heavy-sword-case deficit is retained as an explicit uncalibrated-mass/support-box residual; the animation is not certified for an assigned 6% sword mass.

## lunge_thrust — completed

64 frames / 2.133 seconds. F1–15 load and ground push; F16–30 airborne; F31 lands into the committed thrust. The body passes the marked target at Y=−1.8 m and continues into BACK TO PLAYER. No neutral-return tail: endpoint speed is 0.306 m/s, facing is 146.64° away from the target and the trailing blade's forward-axis dot product is −0.843. The F64 pose is identical to the pre-L01 blend on all 121 bones.

### L01 — recovery retiming fix

Freshly sampled the actual pre-fix blend, SHA256 `5644b867b5eafa282eb47a94ff893ac0ed57009ee9299624b3e2883b89b0be9f`, and reproduced the independent report. Quaternion-log measurements use 253 quarter-frame samples, shortest rotations, interval-ending frame labels, and degrees/frame at 30 fps. The numbers below cover the **whole clip**, so a later peak cannot hide outside the recovery window.

